      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Thomas Karatzas</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/karatzas_thomas">@karatzas_thomas</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960">http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960">http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>Did someone say … cookies?<br/>X and third parties integrated by X use cookies to provide you with a better, safer and faster service and to support our business. Some cookies are necessary to use our services, improve our services, and make sure they work properly. Show more about your choices.<br/>Accept all cookies<br/>Refuse non-essential cookies<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJxXtwJXYAAi4K2?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960/karatzas%5Fthomas/article/2061840456992919997/media/2061619172958756864)<br/>How we re-invented Workflow Builders using Modal Sandboxes<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1960053835717632000/RIqTPsQd_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960/karatzas%5Fthomas)<br/>[Thomas Karatzas](http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960/karatzas%5Fthomas)<br/>[@karatzas\_thomas](http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960/karatzas%5Fthomas)<br/>·<br/>20h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow karatzas\_thomas<br/>5<br/>48<br/>[22K](http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960/karatzas%5Fthomas/status/2061840456992919997/analytics)<br/>We rebuilt the workflow builder from scratch, for the coding agent era.<br/>[Terse](https://www.useterse.ai/)<br/> is automation that lives where developers do. Build, debug, and deploy complex agentic workflows from your terminal or IDE. Serverless hosting, scaling, and observability come standard.<br/>## <br/>TLDR of Terse Architecture<br/>Terse is a code-first Workflow/Automation builder. Every organization in Terse can have multiple <br/>[projects](https://docs.useterse.ai/core-concepts/projects)<br/>. Each project, is a npm package that contains multiple Jobs. A <br/>[Job](https://docs.useterse.ai/core-concepts/jobs)<br/>, is a set of triggers + a closure that is run when a trigger fires. Closures contain multiple action steps and <br/>[TerseAgents](https://docs.useterse.ai/core-concepts/terse-agent)<br/>. Of course, all of this is defined in pure Typescript.<br/>## <br/>Requirements<br/>Hosting is a key feature for us. In the age of AI, we must:<br/>1. Run un-trusted 3P code on behalf of our users<br/>2. Run agents in the cloud safely<br/>3. Pause execution and resume (Human in the Loop)<br/>4. Be able to scale easily with demand<br/>5. Be serverless (don’t want to force users to have set up hosting to get started)<br/>That’s when I came across this <br/>[blog post](https://modal.com/blog/lovable-case-study)<br/> mentioning how Lovable is fully powered by Modal’s Sandboxes as well as the famous <br/>[Ramp one](https://modal.com/blog/how-ramp-built-a-full-context-background-coding-agent-on-modal)<br/> in January. Looks like Modal Sandboxes was the obvious choice!<br/>I remember building the core of the SDK and thinking in back of my mind this sandbox piece was going to kill me. After all, hosting is usually the hardest part right?<br/>In reality, it took about an hour to get spun up. I was shocked.<br/>Let’s walk through my original POC and how I made job startup 100x faster by utilizing the full gamut of Modal’s sandbox API.<br/>## <br/>The Implementation<br/>The original was indeed a bit rough, but deployments took less than a second. It looked something like:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJvz9XzXwAAbw3J?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960/karatzas%5Fthomas/article/2061840456992919997/media/2061509490139185152)<br/>Unfortunately, this creates a pretty complex flow at trigger runtime:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJv0D1-WgAAC_Kx?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2061507690258472960/karatzas%5Fthomas/article/2061840456992919997/media/2061509601317519360)<br/>The code for the Modal part was very elegant:<br/>typescript<br/>```typescript<br/>// this part is super fast<br/>const app = await modal.apps.fromName("terse-sdk-sandbox", { createIfMissing: true })<br/>const image = modal.images.fromRegistry("node:22-slim")<br/>const sb = await modal.sandboxes.create(app, image)<br/>// Writ</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 48 · 🔁 2 · 🔖 80</p><p><a href="https://x.com/karatzas_thomas/status/2061840456992919997">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
