      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>AlphaSignal AI</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/AlphaSignalAI">@AlphaSignalAI</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488">http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488</a></p></blockquote><div><img src="https://iii.dev/og-image.png" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://opengraph.githubassets.com/2ffc25676d9c927b79720c3156f17a469eb8325938d8eb60b6775af74170306a/iii-hq/iii" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/raw/main/.github/assets/zero-integration.png" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/92a4a049f70f8d8154d79043ee9c840b50767301fab92a5ca2d3efab7f839655/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f656e67696e652d454c76322d626c75652e737667" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/e5ba10dd430a64180e2a1828c43f8b109dcac5777584149b0122f7a7ce2c60cf/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f73646b2d4170616368652d2d322e302d677265656e2e737667" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/f289518dccc1f4ff4755114de445e26499d2acc7dc8358efa2e952561e1eba85/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f646f636b65722f762f6969696465762f6969693f6c6162656c3d646f636b6572" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/75727243b0716941c6c5904996f51f9bf3d8d934cf2758ee24c23899e7b270a6/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6e706d2f762f6969692d73646b3f6c6162656c3d6e706d" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/25611792a9ea5c03ff0776921fa359b9bb3ee014a3e4340684181837cec4c4fe/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f707970692f762f6969692d73646b3f6c6162656c3d70797069" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/></div><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488">http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJvU6bqaoAEC7AA?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488/AlphaSignalAI/article/2061475977902125342/media/2061475354775298049)<br/>A New Model for Backend Infrastructure <br/>[![Square profile picture](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2014100845189529600/Ff1Xc28-_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>[AlphaSignal AI](http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>[@AlphaSignalAI](http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>·<br/>9h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow AlphaSignalAI<br/>1<br/>4<br/>27<br/>[2.6K](http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488/AlphaSignalAI/status/2061475977902125342/analytics)<br/># <br/>Why your Python pipeline and TypeScript API can't call each other, and how one runtime fixes that<br/>&gt; In \~8 minutes learn why today's backends accumulate integration debt, and how iii replaces those integrations with a single shared runtime.<br/>When you add a new capability to your backend, you pay an integration tax. Every time.<br/>Want a queue? Pick a vendor, write an adapter, configure retries. Want observability?<br/>Another SDK, another config, another set of traces isolated from everything else. Want an agent harness?<br/>Separate retry model, separate timeout config, a deployment story that has nothing to do with your existing services.<br/>By the time a mid-size backend has a queue, cron, an HTTP layer, a state store, and an agent, each one was integrated manually against the others. <br/>They don't share a trace format, a retry semantic, or a way to directly call each other's functions. The stack is held together by bespoke glue.<br/>iii is a bet that this problem is architectural, not operational. The answer isn't better integrations. It's a shared runtime that makes integration unnecessary in the first place.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJu4EQrbIAAVAQg?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488/AlphaSignalAI/article/2061475977902125342/media/2061443637788221440)<br/>## <br/>The problem iii is trying to solve<br/>Traditional backend architectures integrate point-to-point.<br/>Service A calls Service B through a dedicated HTTP client. Service B publishes to a queue that Service C subscribes to. Service D writes metrics to an observability platform that none of the others can read from directly.<br/>Every new service creates new integrations against every existing service. The complexity doesn't grow linearly, it grows with the square of the number of services. A five-service stack might have ten integrations. A twenty-service stack might have close to two hundred.<br/>Most teams don't feel this as a single crisis. They feel it as constant friction: a new tool takes weeks to wire up, an agent needs a separate orchestration harness, tests break when one dependency changes its interface, and nobody can trace a request end-to-end because traces live in five different systems.<br/>iii's claim is that the integration surface itself is the problem. Not any specific integration.<br/>## <br/>The shared runtime model<br/>iii introduces a single engine that every service connects to over WebSocket. Once connected, any service can call any named function in any other connected service, regardless of language, location, or deployment environment.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJvJ-i3bcAAgXdt?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2061443362943807488/AlphaSignalAI/article/2061475977902125342/media/2061463330800496640)<br/>Adding a new service doesn't create N new integrations. It creates one new WebSocket connection, and everything already connected can reach it immediately. The engine handles routing, serialization, and delivery.<br/>The repo has shipped continuously: 1,694 commits, 225 releases, v0.16.1 on May 29, 2026\. The engine is 74.8% Rust. The SDKs are thin connectors, not framewo</blockquote><p>🔗 <a href="https://iii.dev/">iii — Three primitives. Zero integration cost.</a></p><p>🔗 <a href="https://github.com/iii-hq/iii">GitHub - iii-hq/iii: Effortlessly compose, extend, and observe every service in real-time for the first time ever. · GitHub</a></p><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 65 · 🔁 8 · 💬 1 · 🔖 130</p><p><a href="https://x.com/AlphaSignalAI/status/2061475977902125342">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
