      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Din</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/DinScales26">@DinScales26</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715">http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715">http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJl--aTX0AMrqyN?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715/DinScales26/article/2060819226248818884/media/2060817915176275971)<br/>how to actually get good B2B dealflow from cold outbound...<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2004607244667658240/Nca2FK2__normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715/DinScales26)<br/>[Din](http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715/DinScales26)<br/>[@DinScales26](http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715/DinScales26)<br/>·<br/>18h<br/>·<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow DinScales26<br/>3<br/>4<br/>35<br/>[3.4K](http://x.com/i/article/2059654105816051715/DinScales26/status/2060819226248818884/analytics)<br/>the reason a lot of b2b companies get nothing from cold outbound is they treat it like a volume game<br/>they export a list from apollo, write a generic template, send 10,000 emails, and pray for 1% reply rates lol<br/>the result is a handful of complete shit replies from people who were never going to buy and a pipeline full of NOTHING<br/>consistent deal flow from cold outbound requires getting three things right simultaneously. <br/>if any one of them is broken, the whole system produces nothing...<br/>## <br/>1\. finding people who are already looking<br/>the list is fucking everything<br/>a perfect message sent to the wrong person gets zero replies and a mediocre message sent to the right person gets meetings booked<br/>the mistake most companies make is sourcing leads from static databases. <br/>apollo and zoominfo give you contact information but they DO NOT tell you who's actively looking for a solution right now<br/>so you need intent signals layered on top of contact data...<br/>* companies hiring for roles related to your service are telling you exactly what they need<br/>"hiring head of demand gen" means they don't have one yet, marketing is probably a mess, and they need pipeline help. <br/>"hiring 10 sdrs" means they need the pipeline those sdrs are supposed to generate. <br/>job postings are PUBLICLY available buying signals that almost nobody in cold outbound is using systematically<br/>* companies that just raised funding are actively buying services.<br/>series a companies are building their go to market<br/>series b companies are scaling their sales infrastructure<br/>the yc startup directory is public, crunchbase has free tiers, and sec edgar filings are completely free. <br/>these companies have cash, they have urgency, AND they need vendors<br/>* prospects who are active on linkedin in the last 30 days are actually present on the platform s<br/>so filtering for recent activity eliminates the 40-50% of your list that never checks linkedin and will never see your message<br/>this single filter can double your effective reply rate overnight<br/>* competitors' followers and customers are the highest intent leads possible<br/>because they already understand the problem and are already paying for a solution, <br/>they just need a reason to switch. <br/>we've seen 300% more positive responses from outreach to competitor followers compared to cold lists<br/>the difference between a list that produces 1% reply rates and one that produces 10%+ is ENTIRELY about whether the people on it have signaled they care about what you're selling<br/>## <br/>1\. making them actually reply<br/>the message has to do two things in under 25 words: - prove you can solve their problem - and make it effortless to say yes<br/>* the case study lead works CONSISTENTLY across every vertical we've tested<br/>"we booked 30 calls for a marketing agency in 5 weeks. 2 signed retainer clients. worth a quick conversation?"<br/>the prospect reads this and their brain immediately calculates whether a similar result would be valuable for their business<br/>if it would, they reply and if it wouldn't, they don't. there's no convincing required<br/>* relevance is the only form of personalization that moves the needle<br/>don't mention their</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 45 · 🔁 3 · 💬 3 · 🔖 121</p><p><a href="https://x.com/DinScales26/status/2060819226248818884">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
