## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJfTHz9W4AIslgI?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/borkodotfun/article/2060350372233769261/media/2060347485705396226) Autonomous Capital [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2060467340639092737/49CCI7JH_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/borkodotfun)...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Borko</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/borkodotfun">@borkodotfun</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968">http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968">http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJfTHz9W4AIslgI?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/borkodotfun/article/2060350372233769261/media/2060347485705396226)<br/>Autonomous Capital<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2060467340639092737/49CCI7JH_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/borkodotfun)<br/>[Borko](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/borkodotfun)<br/>[@borkodotfun](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/borkodotfun)<br/>·<br/>18h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow borkodotfun<br/>3<br/>7<br/>63<br/>[1.7K](http://x.com/i/article/2060342141381971968/borkodotfun/status/2060350372233769261/analytics)<br/>AI agents will become real economic actors in finance.<br/>Not because finance is easy. But because finance is already the closest thing we have to a machine-native environment: markets are digital, assets are programmable, APIs exist, prices update continuously, decisions are measurable, and execution can happen without waiting for the physical world.<br/>This is the reason I think the conversation around “AI trading bots” is too small. The important shift is not that users will ask chatbots what to buy. The important shift is that capital itself will become increasingly autonomous.<br/>By autonomous capital, I mean capital that can be monitored, routed, hedged, allocated, and executed by intelligent systems operating within user-defined constraints.<br/>Most financial software today still assumes a human is the operating system. The trader opens five dashboards, checks funding, scans liquidations, reads news, looks at open interest, checks wallet balances, calculates exposure, updates their thesis, manages margin, and then manually executes. Even in crypto, where the rails are programmable, the workflow is still fragmented and human-driven.<br/>The market is composable. The trader’s workflow is not.<br/>That mismatch creates the opportunity.<br/>If AI agents are going to manage financial actions, they need more than a chat interface. They need a structured understanding of the world they are operating in. In finance, that means continuously understanding both market state and portfolio state.<br/>Market state includes things like funding rates, open interest, liquidations, order books, volatility, macro events, smart-money flows, prediction markets, and execution conditions.<br/>Portfolio state includes the user’s positions, collateral, liquidation risk, exposure across venues, trading history, strategy intent, risk tolerance, and behavioral patterns.<br/>Most products understand one side badly, or both sides separately.<br/>A trading terminal may know the market but not the user. A portfolio tracker may know the wallet but not the current opportunity. A chatbot may explain a chart but not understand the trader’s full exposure. An exchange may show liquidation price but not whether adding to a position destroys the user’s actual risk profile.<br/>The missing layer is the system that understands all of this together.<br/>That is what makes the category more interesting than “AI trade ideas.”<br/>A generic trading signal says: buy ETH.<br/>A portfolio-aware financial agent says: given your current BTC exposure, funding environment, collateral usage, execution costs, volatility regime, and recent trading behavior, increasing this position improves or worsens your objective by this amount.<br/>That difference matters.<br/>The first useful agents in finance will not be magical black boxes that predict every move. They will be systems that compress context, enforce discipline, and manage execution better than humans can under pressure.<br/>They will help users answer questions like:<br/>\- Am I actually underexposed, or am I emotionally trying to win back a loss?<br/>\- What happens to my liquidation risk if I add here?<br/>\- Should I cut immediately, scale out, or TWAP over time?<br/>\- Is this funding spread still</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 91 · 🔁 7 · 💬 3 · 🔖 11</p><p><a href="https://x.com/borkodotfun/status/2060350372233769261">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
