## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJeJdGUb0AAGC9x?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/AlphaSignalAI/article/2060361091474223504/media/2060266487550824448) Dynamic Workflows vs Skills vs Subagents: What are the differences? [![Square profile...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>AlphaSignal AI</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/AlphaSignalAI">@AlphaSignalAI</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800">http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800">http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJeJdGUb0AAGC9x?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/AlphaSignalAI/article/2060361091474223504/media/2060266487550824448)<br/>Dynamic Workflows vs Skills vs Subagents: What are the differences?<br/>[![Square profile picture](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2014100845189529600/Ff1Xc28-_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>[AlphaSignal AI](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>[@AlphaSignalAI](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>·<br/>10h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow AlphaSignalAI<br/>6<br/>34<br/>[8.5K](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/AlphaSignalAI/status/2060361091474223504/analytics)<br/>Anthropic just dropped a new orchestration feature called <br/>[Dynamic Workflows](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/workflows)<br/> which can spawn hundreds of subagents to take on massive tasks.<br/>It lets Claude write a script that fires off subagents, runs them in parallel, and hands you back one checked result.<br/>But how exactly does it work, and how does it differ from the other agentic development approaches using subagents and skills?<br/>According to the internal team at Anthropic, they built this feature a couple months ago, and it has slowly become their daily driver.<br/>## <br/>What is a Dynamic Workflow?<br/>This feature lets Claude write a script that fires off subagents, runs them in parallel, and hands you back one checked result.<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2044472418815893504/xf14RxM8_normal.png)](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/ClaudeDevs)<br/>ClaudeDevs<br/>![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1798110641414443008/XP8gyBaY_bigger.jpg)<br/>@ClaudeDevs<br/>·<br/>[May 28](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/ClaudeDevs/status/2060044853279617150)<br/>New in Claude Code (research preview): dynamic workflows. Claude writes an orchestration script on the fly, then spins up a large fleet of coordinated subagents in parallel to take on your most complex tasks. Use the word "workflow" in a prompt to get started.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJa_ctabIAA84so?format=png&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/ClaudeDevs/status/2060044853279617150/photo/1)<br/>302<br/>1.2K<br/>9.7K<br/>[3.1M](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/ClaudeDevs/status/2060044853279617150/analytics)<br/>It was released alongside the Claude Opus 4.8 which is more capable: SWE-bench Pro (from 64.3 to 69.2) and noticeably more honest about its own work.<br/>Type “workflow” into a prompt and Claude writes an orchestration plan, then follows it to the letter.<br/>That strict plan is the point. Every stage runs in the right order, even across hundreds of agents.<br/>One run can fan out wide, but not infinitely. Anthropic caps it at 16 agents running at once and 1,000 total per workflow.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJeJ10CaAAAkBQ_?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/AlphaSignalAI/article/2060361091474223504/media/2060266912140099584)<br/>&gt; Note: Dynamic Workflows are in research preview. They run in the Claude Code CLI, Desktop, and VS Code extension, plus the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, Google Cloud Vertex AI, and Microsoft Foundry. They’re on by default for Max, Team, and API users. On Enterprise, an admin turns them on first.<br/>You also need Claude Code v2.1.154 or later to see the feature at all.<br/>## <br/>Subagents vs Skill vs Dynamic Workflows<br/>Subagents and skills both shipped in earlier Claude Code updates. So what does a workflow add?<br/>It comes down to who holds the plan.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJeJ5GzaUAArThV?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2060265616859340800/AlphaSignalAI/article/2060361091474223504/media/2060266968717086720)<br/>A subagent leaves Claude in charge. It decides which worker to spawn next, tur</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 66 · 🔁 11 · 💬 1 · 🔖 167</p><p><a href="https://x.com/AlphaSignalAI/status/2060361091474223504">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
